The Documentation branch is responsible for maintaining clear, organized, and up-to-date documentation for the Event Management System. Its purpose is to provide developers, contributors, organizers, administrators, and other project members with all the necessary information required to understand, use, develop, and maintain the system effectively.

This branch contains important project information such as system features, project structure, installation instructions, configuration requirements, development guidelines, module descriptions, API documentation, database information, and contribution guidelines. It acts as a central knowledge base for the entire project.

The Documentation branch can also include detailed information about individual modules such as the Frontend, Backend, Designer, Organizer, Treasurer, Admin, and Attendee branches. Each module can have its responsibilities, functionality, dependencies, workflows, and development requirements properly documented.

Technical documentation may include API endpoints, request and response formats, authentication procedures, database models, environment variables, deployment instructions, and troubleshooting information. This makes it easier for developers to understand how different components communicate and how new features can be added without affecting existing functionality.

The branch can also maintain project guidelines related to Git workflow, branch naming, commit conventions, pull requests, coding standards, and contribution procedures. Keeping these guidelines documented helps maintain consistency across the development team.

Overall, the Documentation branch ensures that important project knowledge is properly recorded and easily accessible. Its goal is to improve collaboration, reduce confusion, simplify onboarding for new contributors, and make the Event Management System easier to develop, maintain, and scale over time.
